{#- Browser view of the same data as scan-report.txt.j2. Deliberately one
    self-contained file with no external CSS, JS, font or image: this page is
    served by a static file server with no network access of its own, and it
    is read exactly when something is wrong, which is the worst time to depend
    on a CDN. -#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>homelab security scan</title>
<style>
  :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
  body { font: 15px/1.55 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
         margin: 0 auto; max-width: 62rem; padding: 2rem 1.25rem 4rem; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.35rem; margin: 0 0 .25rem; }
  .sub { opacity: .7; margin: 0 0 1.75rem; font-size: .9rem; }
  .cards { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .75rem; margin-bottom: 1.75rem; }
  .card { border: 1px solid currentColor; border-radius: .5rem; padding: .7rem 1rem;
          min-width: 8rem; opacity: .95; }
  .card .n { font-size: 1.8rem; font-weight: 700; display: block; line-height: 1.1; }
  .card .l { font-size: .75rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; opacity: .75; }
  .crit .n { color: #c0392b; }
  .imp .n  { color: #b9770e; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: .5rem 0 2rem; }
  th, td { text-align: right; padding: .4rem .6rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(128,128,128,.35); }
  th:first-child, td:first-child { text-align: left; }
  th { font-size: .75rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em; opacity: .75; }
  .bad { color: #c0392b; font-weight: 700; }
  .note { border-left: 3px solid rgba(128,128,128,.5); padding: .1rem 0 .1rem 1rem;
          margin: 1.5rem 0; opacity: .85; font-size: .9rem; }
  .banner { border: 1px solid #c0392b; border-radius: .5rem; padding: .75rem 1rem;
            margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  a { color: inherit; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>homelab security scan</h1>
<p class="sub">{{ ansible_date_time.iso8601 }} &middot; report-only &mdash; this run installed, upgraded and restarted nothing</p>

{% if scan_broken | length > 0 %}
<div class="banner">
  <strong>{{ scan_broken | join(', ') }} could not be scanned.</strong><br>
  A host that could not be asked is not a host with nothing pending. Treat the
  numbers below as a floor, not a total.
</div>
{% endif %}

<div class="cards">
  <div class="card"><span class="n">{{ scan_total }}</span><span class="l">pending errata</span></div>
  <div class="card crit"><span class="n">{{ scan_critical }}</span><span class="l">critical</span></div>
  <div class="card imp"><span class="n">{{ scan_important }}</span><span class="l">important</span></div>
  <div class="card"><span class="n">{{ scan_ok | length }}/{{ groups['service_vms'] | length }}</span><span class="l">hosts answered</span></div>
</div>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>host</th><th>total</th><th>critical</th><th>important</th><th>moderate</th><th>low</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
{% for host in groups['service_vms'] | sort %}
{%   set f = scan_findings[host] | default({}) %}
{%   if f.ok | default(false) | bool %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ host }}</td>
      <td>{{ f.total }}</td>
      <td{{ ' class="bad"' if (f.critical | int) > 0 else '' }}>{{ f.critical }}</td>
      <td>{{ f.important }}</td>
      <td>{{ f.moderate }}</td>
      <td>{{ f.low }}</td>
    </tr>
{%   else %}
    <tr><td>{{ host }}</td><td colspan="5" class="bad">NOT SCANNED &mdash; {{ f.detail | default('no result recorded') }}</td></tr>
{%   endif %}
{% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<p>
  Previous run total: <strong>{{ scan_previous.total | default('none — first run') }}</strong> &middot;
  Escalated to alerts: <strong>{{ 'YES — ' ~ scan_escalation_reason if scan_escalate | bool else 'no' }}</strong>
</p>

<p><a href="latest.txt">latest.txt</a> &middot; <a href="state.json">state.json</a></p>

<div class="note">
  <p><strong>What this means.</strong> Nothing in this estate updates itself. That is
  a deliberate trade recorded in <code>docs/unattended.md</code>: packages install on
  demand and images are digest-pinned, so nothing shifts underneath while nobody is
  watching. The cost of that trade is the number at the top of this page, and the
  reason this scan exists is that the number was previously unknown rather than
  accepted.</p>
  <p>Acting on it is a manual decision this job will never take for you. Applying
  errata is dnf's security-only upgrade path, run on the host by hand, followed by
  the reboot a kernel or glibc advisory usually requires.</p>
</div>

<div class="note">
  <p><strong>This page is not a secret, and it should be.</strong> The Authelia login in
  front of <code>scan.{{ service_domain }}</code> protects the hostname, not the
  service: this same content is served unauthenticated on
  <code>{{ hostvars[infra_host].ansible_host }}:8085</code> to anything on the LAN
  or the tailnet. That is an accepted risk, recorded in
  <code>docs/automation-opportunities.md</code>.</p>
</div>

</body>
</html>
